# xterm with 24-bit colour, for Emacs's terminal frames (see docs/cmd.md).
# Emacs takes 24-bit colour from a terminal's terminfo entry (setf24/setb24),
# or from COLORTERM=truecolor in its own environment: a server started
# elsewhere (the GUI app) doesn't have the client's, so its terminal frames
# got 256 colours. cmd/diff compiles this into ~/.terminfo when needed:
#   tic -x -o ~/.terminfo cmd/xterm-24bit.terminfo
xterm-24bit|xterm with 24-bit direct colour,
	use=xterm-256color,
	setb24=\E[48;2;%p1%{65536}%/%d;%p1%{256}%/%{255}%&%d;%p1%{255}%&%dm,
	setf24=\E[38;2;%p1%{65536}%/%d;%p1%{256}%/%{255}%&%d;%p1%{255}%&%dm,
